    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense faces a critical slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the lineup with a stellar 74.74 projection against Cole. Despite the opponent's pedigree, the park factors and **Henderson**\u2019s dynamic platoon advantage generate a clear green light for our primary power threat. He is joined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) as the core drivers for today\u2019s production. **Antonacci** remains a priority start, leveraging his leadoff status and a favorable matchup against the vulnerable arm of Holmes. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (65.99) benefits from a strong park factor and a mid-tier matchup against Bradish; while his base projection is moderate, the overall environment pushes him well into the strong-start category required for our Roto climb.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just shy of our threshold at a 37.99 efficiency score. While **Nunez** remains a vital asset for our stolen base strategy\u2014given his elite 50% hold\u2014the sheer strength of deGrom\u2019s peripherals forced his benching to preserve our limited game caps. We are also navigating the continued absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill**, which necessitates a high-efficiency approach from the healthy starters we have deployed. Managers should monitor **Drake Baldwin** (64.69) closely; his score is buoyed by a favorable xwOBA, but Kay\u2019s 4.52 xERA suggests a volatile outing. With no major weather concerns currently flagged, the objective is to maximize the offensive output from our top four slots while maintaining strict discipline regarding the bench threshold to ensure we do not burn starts on sub-40 efficiency plays.",
